  "description": "1.  Leyland cypress: reduce width on the gate side and front by 1-1.5m (not left side). 2. Cotoneaster frigidus: reduce lateral growth over garden back to remove overhang to bed. 3. Flowering cherry: crown reduce back to the previous, most recent reduction points.\r4. 2 x Leyland cypress:  reduce height to level of adjacent mews roof & take back branches in line with lawn border to allow more light to flower bed. 5. Ilex aquifolium: reduce height by 50%. 6. Sambucus nigra: re-pollard. 7. Sycamore (left side of electricity sub-station): reduce branches above public footpath by up to 3m and prune back to boundary. 8. Sycamore (right side of electricity sub-station): crown reduce back to previous, most recent reduction points. 9. 2 x Laurus nobilis: reduce all round by 1-1.5m give light to the shrubs underneath. 10. 5 x London plane: crown reduce back to the previous, most recent reduction points. 11. 2 x lime: crown reduce to the previous, most recent reduction points, retaining selected shortened furnishing growth and at least 50% of remaining fine branch structure for crown continuity. 13. 2 x sycamore: crown reduce back to the previous, most recent reduction points. \r",
